{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PHASE 2 (execution — continuation of the crashed session; ticket held in_progress by this host bot, claimed_session=null). Operator-approved scope: Remedy 1 (telemetry) + Remedy 2 (shared-prefix cache breakpoint). Not pursuing cross-ticket prefix identity or disabling caching on single-step passes.\n\nRE-SCOPE of AC 2 (\"the marked prefix for a given pass is byte-identical across TICKETS, pinned by a test verified RED\"): WITHDRAWN as unsatisfiable, per this ticket's own Phase-1 investigation (b).2 and (c).3. The marked prefix embeds the whole plan BY DESIGN (shared_plan_prefix = stance preamble + full plan; stories 0250/8415/9374/25fa build on that placement); content-addressed caching therefore cannot reuse a plan-bearing prefix across DIFFERENT plans, and bug f81d (wont-fix) already disproved the move-plan-to-user-message alternative at the mechanism level. Cross-ticket identity would require evicting the plan from the marked prefix, which destroys the within-run container/chunk reuse warm-then-fan-out depends on.\n\nAC 2 is REPLACED by an in-session-achievable AC: the marked cache breakpoint lands at the END of the byte-identical shared_plan_prefix boundary (not after the pass-specific stance suffix), pinned by an OFFLINE unit test against real pydantic-ai _map_message for BOTH the anthropic and bedrock cache styles, so within one run the finder cache WRITE is READ by the Pass-2 verifier and a same-ticket re-review inside the TTL reads too.\n\nMechanism (verified offline): pydantic-ai's anthropic_cache_instructions / bedrock_cache_instructions place the system cache_control on the LAST STATIC block; a DYNAMIC instruction after a static system block moves the breakpoint to the end of that static block. So: pass shared_plan_prefix as the system_prompt (static) and the pass-specific stance suffix as a DYNAMIC instruction — the model still receives prefix+suffix byte-identically (behaviour-preserving; only the cache boundary moves). Delivered via a new RunRequest.cache_prefix runner-seam knob assembled in agent_call.build_agent_kwargs; wired into the Pass-1 finder (writes) and the Pass-2 verifier workflow step (reads), plus the prerequisite_verifier template reordered to LEAD with {{shared_prefix}} (fidelity-checked). Remedy 1: warn_if_cache_ineffective gains a write>0/read==0 aggregate detector. Live A/B minimised per operator direction; hit proven via the offline breakpoint-boundary test + render diff."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785867969193910001,"uuid":"e5994189-1b18-4db0-8983-7f26eb36320e"}